        "title": "Docs: Document persistent build cache for Freebuff web CI lane",
        "summary": "The CI testing documentation was updated to explain that the Freebuff web build lane now uses a persistent Turbopack build cache instead of compiling from scratch. This is managed by scripts/render-next-cache.mjs, which stashes the .next/cache directory in $RUNNER_TEMP during GitHub Actions runs, and is scoped by bun.lock and next.config.mjs. The notes include a measured 2026-10-07 result where compile time halved from 112s to 56s, and clarify that build-web does not use this cache because its cold compile is under 30s.",
